CICFlowMeter-MG
===============

This repository is an unofficial fork of CICFlowMeter.

Upstream project
----------------
CICFlowMeter (formerly ISCXFlowMeter)
Developed at the Canadian Institute for Cybersecurity, University of New Brunswick.
  https://github.com/ahlashkari/CICFlowMeter
  https://github.com/CanadianInstituteForCybersecurity/CICFlowMeter

This fork as a whole is licensed under GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE.txt). The reason is
that the fat jars below bundle Weka (GPL-2.0) and jnetpcap (GPL-3 / LGPL-3), so
the combined binary is a GPL work. Upstream CICFlowMeter is MIT licensed; its
notice is preserved verbatim in LICENSES/MIT-CICFlowMeter.txt and applies to the
upstream-derived parts.

Upstream authors and contributors, as listed in the upstream LICENSE.txt:
  Arash Habibi Lashkari     - researcher and developer (founder)
  Gerard Drapper Gil        - researcher and developer (co-founder)
  Muhammad Saiful Islam     - researcher and developer (co-founder)

The first 108 commits in this repository's history are upstream's work and are
kept with their original authors. Upstream's MIT licence text lives unmodified in
LICENSES/MIT-CICFlowMeter.txt.

If you use this tool in academic work, cite the upstream papers listed in
LICENSE.txt / README.md.

